\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Does adding witnessed symmetric choice to choiceless polynomial time with counting strictly increase the Boolean queries definable on all finite structures, even when one total sentence uses only one witnessed-choice occurrence?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Does adding witnessed symmetric choice to choiceless polynomial time with counting strictly increase the Boolean queries definable on all finite structures, even when one total sentence uses only one witnessed-choice occurrence?

